<h1>Week 27</h1>

<p><strong>From:</strong> Lana</p>
<p><strong>Artist:</strong> Dramarama</p>
<p><strong>Album:</strong> <em>Dramarama</em></p>

<p>Kayla,</p>

<p>
I am so excited that I figured out how to get this one to you. It is one of my favorite albums. I was able to put all but the last three songs not available anywhere. ☹️ Next time you are in my car I will play them for you.
</p>

<p>
This is Dramarama. It is surprising because the song <em>Anything, Anything</em> was so popular at Grafittis. I can remember our group running around dancing to this song and singing so loud. It might be one of my favorite songs ever, it is crazy good.
</p>

<p>
But what is surprising is how beautiful, real and profound their other songs are.
</p>

<p>
I honestly love them all but standout favorites:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Emerald City</li>
<li>Last Cigarette</li>
<li>What Are We Gonna Do</li>
<li>Work For Food</li>
<li>Incredible (always makes me think of Laura and her need to have music or TV on at all times)</li>
<li>Senseless Fun (makes me think of you, me, and Chloe at different times of our individual lives and how hard life can be and the feelings of despair)</li>
</ul>

<p>
This one is so special to me. I am so relieved that I figured something out. My list would not be complete without this one for sure.
</p>

<p>
Love you,
</p>

<p>
Mom
</p>

